# Postman sync

**On-demand only.** Do **not** sync Postman as a side effect of adding or changing endpoints. Run `check-endpoint` / `upsert-endpoint` only when the user explicitly asks to sync, check, or update Postman.

When asked, update the Postman collection through the **full** Postman MCP in `.cursor/mcp.json`. Do not hand-edit collections. Management-tab cards (`data_visualization/static/data_visualization/js/management.js` `ENDPOINTS`) stay a normal part of endpoint work — they are separate from Postman sync.

## Collection target

This repo maps to **one** Postman collection in workspace **Perso**. Collection name: **`market-watch`**. The whole collection is this project (no extra parent folder). Nested folders still follow each `/` in the path — see `check-endpoint` / `upsert-endpoint`.

Machine-specific workspace/collection IDs live in **`.cursor/postman.local.json`** (gitignored).

**Lookup order** (skills / sync):

1. `.cursor/postman.local.json` if it exists — use `workspace` / `collection` (prefer `id` / `uid` when set). Honor any extra keys on that machine.
2. Else search Postman for workspace name `Perso` and collection name `market-watch`.
3. If several collections still match, list them and ask — do not guess.

Shared defaults when a field is omitted locally:

- Workspace name: `Perso`
- Collection name: `market-watch`
- Local API: http://127.0.0.1:8000/
- OpenAPI: http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/docs/

**MCP vs collection identity:**

- **MCP** (how Cursor talks to Postman) is `.cursor/mcp.json`: full profile `https://mcp.postman.com/mcp`. OAuth is per machine automatically.
- **Target** (which workspace/collection to edit) is `.cursor/postman.local.json`.
- If this PC needs a different MCP server (EU URL, API key, extra servers), put it in **`~/.cursor/mcp.json`** so it stays off git. Do not commit secrets. A `mcp` key in `postman.local.json` is advisory only; Cursor does not read that file for MCP.

## Sync steps

1. Resolve the target with the lookup order above.
2. Use `check-endpoint` for a read-only drift report.
3. Use `upsert-endpoint` to create or update matching requests (never delete orphaned ones — move them into a collection-root `Deprecated` folder).
4. If write tools are missing, the MCP is not on the `/mcp` (full) profile — stop and switch the URL to `https://mcp.postman.com/mcp` (or override in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` on this PC).
5. Body conventions: non-multipart bodies are **JSON** (raw language `json` / CLI `-d 'json:...'`), never Text; **do not** set a manual `Content-Type` header — Postman detects it. Always sync query + URI params from the Django route / serializers.
6. Docs tab: every request needs markdown with an opening summary plus (when applicable) `## Path Parameters`, `## Query Parameters`, `## Request Body`, `## Example Payload`, `## Response`, and `## Example Response`. Generate from OpenAPI via `scripts/generate_postman_docs.py` when possible.

Folder placement follows each `/` in the path; skip path-param segments. See `check-endpoint` / `upsert-endpoint`.
